  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "23. Aircraft",
    "ruleNumber": "23.02",
    "summary": "AIRCRAFT units have just one move type available: the Ingress move. As the opposing player’s turn ends, send any of your AIRCRAFT units still on the table back to Strategic Reserves. Moving models can pass through AIRCRAFT models. Without FLY for its Surge, Consolidation or Pile-In move, a unit ignores AIRCRAFT when choosing enemy units and checking which enemy is closest. Being Engaged only with AIRCRAFT leaves a unit eligible for a Normal move or an Advance move, subject to the other requirements of those moves.",
